import ../../site/games/farm/annotations.dl
import site_fixture.dl

set instance to an instance of website fixture
set driver to a website shader test driver
set view to a new UI view
set view's driver to the address of driver
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's view to the address of view
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
set state's farm's document to the initial website farm document
set document to state's farm's document
set role to the item at 0 in (document's roles)
set actor to the item at 0 in (document's world's workers)
set source to the string form of "# 🌽\r\nif i can reach it:\r\n    wait"
set role's source to source
set condition to a new website farm instruction
set condition's operation to the website farm test operation
set condition's identifier to 1
set condition's target to the website farm subject target
set condition's destination to 2
set condition's source to @intrinsic("construct", website execution range, true, 1, 0, 1, 17)
set action to the website Farm instruction named "wait"
set action's source to @intrinsic("construct", website execution range, true, 2, 4, 2, 8)
set plan to an empty website farm plan
append condition to plan's code
append action to plan's code
apply website farm plan plan from source to role for actor in (document's world)
set actor's routine's position to 2
set actor's routine's traced to true
set actor's routine's source to action's source
set actor's routine's condition source to condition's source
set actor's routine's condition branch to 1
set actor's routine's message to "Waited."
load website source "Farm source" from source in (the address of state)
set editor to the UI source editor labeled "Farm source" in (state's language)
set main to editor's document
color UI text source in (editor's node) in (the address of instance)
add UI text color (UI ink 11 22 33) from 0 to 2 in (editor's node) in (the address of instance)
set colors to (the UI value for (editor's node) in (the address of instance))'s colors
set helper to a UI source document named "helper.dl" at "file:///lib/helper.dl" containing "An imported definition" in (main's project)
show UI source document helper in editor in (the address of view)
set {main state} to the UI text state for main in editor in (the address of instance)
mark UI text source in layer "search" at priority 20 in main state
add UI text mark (UI ink 210 170 55) from 0 to 2 with opacity 70 in layer "search" in main state

refresh website Farm annotations in (the address of state)
set execution to the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state
require condition ((execution != (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) and ((execution's marks' start = 32) and (execution's marks' end = 36))) reporting "Farm execution did not map CRLF and Unicode source to editor byte offsets"
set branch to the UI text mark layer named "condition" in main state
require condition ((branch != (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) and ((branch's marks' start = 8) and (branch's marks' end = 25))) reporting "The condition leading to a Farm action has no independent annotation"
require condition ((branch's marks' ink's red = 80) and (execution's marks' ink's red = 104)) reporting "Farm actions and true conditions lost their distinct colors"
require condition ((main state's colors = colors) and ((the UI text mark layer named "search" in main state)'s marks' end = 2)) reporting "Farm execution replaced semantic colors or search results"
require condition (((the UI value for (editor's node) in (the address of instance))'s mark layers) = (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "Farm execution marked the displayed imported file instead of its main source"
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "Farm execution" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "Condition is true. Waited.") reporting "Farm execution did not explain the condition and action"

set actor's routine's source to condition's source
set actor's routine's branch to 0
set actor's routine's condition branch to -1
refresh website Farm annotations in (the address of state)
set execution to the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state
require condition ((execution's marks' start = 8) and (execution's marks' ink's red = 196)) reporting "A false Farm condition did not replace the current instruction annotation"
require condition ((the UI text mark layer named "condition" in main state) = (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "Stepping a condition retained the previous action's condition layer"
set role's source to source + "\r\n# A new draft"
refresh website Farm annotations in (the address of state)
require condition ((the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state) = (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "An edited draft retained execution from its applied source"
require condition ((main state's colors = colors) and ((the UI text mark layer named "search" in main state)'s marks' end = 2)) reporting "Clearing Farm execution removed another editor feature's annotations"
set role's source to source
set role's needs rebuilding to true
refresh website Farm annotations in (the address of state)
require condition ((the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state) = (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "A saved role showed obsolete source ranges before rebuilding"
set role's needs rebuilding to false
set document's selected to "player"
refresh website Farm annotations in (the address of state)
require condition ((the UI text mark layer named "execution" in main state) = (0 as a pointer to UI text mark layer)) reporting "Selecting the player retained another worker's instruction"
free website farm document document
free website farm plan the address of plan
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close the address of instance
print line "Farm execution shares editor mark layers, maps Unicode and CRLF, isolates main-file execution from imports, and clears stale ranges without losing search or colors."
